{
  // Config for the standalone `typecheck` task (tsc --noEmit) — mirrors
  // apps/legacy/tsconfig.typecheck.json, and for the same reason.
  //
  // tsconfig.json includes ".next/types/**/*.ts"; Next.js adds and re-adds that
  // entry itself on every build, so it cannot simply be deleted. Those files are
  // GENERATED by `next build`, and turbo cannot express a same-package
  // build->typecheck edge (`^build` orders upstream workspaces only). So
  // `turbo run typecheck build` ran both concurrently in one workspace and tsc
  // read .next/types while next rewrote it — spurious "error TS6053: File
  // '.next/types/.../page.ts' not found", green or red depending on
  // interleaving. Adding an un-carated same-package "build" to turbo.json's
  // typecheck task was tried and failed CI (commit 26256cc).
  //
  // Dropping ".next" entirely makes typecheck HERMETIC: it reads only
  // checked-in source, shares no file with build, and the race is impossible by
  // construction. No coverage is lost — CI always ran tsc on a fresh checkout
  // with no .next, so that glob matched nothing there anyway, and the generated
  // route types stay validated by `next build`'s own type-check step.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "include": ["next-env.d.ts", "**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", ".next"]
}
